IMPORT prelude

-- REFUSE "reason" marks a case the encoding deliberately does not cover.
-- On main it is a prelude function that type-checks at any type.
-- Only the branches that do not refuse are evaluated here: evaluation that
-- reaches a REFUSE stops with an assumed-term error.

-- A refusal at NUMBER
@export default The fee in a given year
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fee in year` year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2000
    THEN 100
    ELSE REFUSE "this schedule is not encoded for years before 2000"

-- A refusal at BOOLEAN
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the fee is waived in year` year MEANS
    IF year AT LEAST 2000
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE REFUSE "this rule has not been written yet"

#EVAL `the fee in year` 2024
#EVAL `the fee is waived in year` 2024

#ASSERT `the fee in year` 2024 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT NOT `the fee is waived in year` 2024
